            <ArticleTitle>Review of pain associated with minimal endometriosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>5-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Endometriosis has been examined in numerous ways and, primarily, it presents in two forms: painful, often associated with minimal findings; and non-painful, often associated with marked disease. The focus of this review article is to examine the pain aspect associated with minimal endometriosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
